rchitecture and execution constraints","content":"I’m tracking several current constraints: removing legacy routes, adding navigation and collapsible work areas, and building React-based document and annotation workflows with fail-closed data handling and recovery startup.\n\nDeepTutor remains optional rather than foundational. The project is currently integrating OSUI v3 and local material workflows, so I shouldn’t claim full closure until visual, interaction, Windows WebView, and exact-build evidence are complete. External dependencies require centralized registration, and the knowledge lifecycle and frozen execution baseline must remain owner-controlled.","chunks":[],"finished":true},{"summary":"Reviewing verified implementation boundaries","content":"I’m preserving the current architecture: shell and TypeScript/JavaScript UI work continue without a Python-to-Rust rewrite, while native Windows verification remains required because WSL is insufficient. I’m keeping temporary state under the designated project area, avoiding protected drives and credentials, and treating parallel work as branch-based.\n\nThe repository shows mature governance, but several claims remain unverified: native GUI takeover, cold-start behavior, Green replacement, real-library separation, migration, recovery, model resources, and release qualification. The frontend is largely closed on Windows with Avalonia and Python, yet the overall product remains incomplete.","chunks":[],"finished":true},{"summary":"Reviewed project architecture and implementation constraints","content":"","chunks":[],"finished":true}],"source_analysis_msg_id":"91b4476d-fb49-414b-8030-27ef4240eb2e"},"status":"finished_successfully","end_turn":false,"weight":1.0,"metadata":{"reasoning_status":"is_reasoning"},"recipient":"all","channel":null},{"id":"87f0280e-0a91-4a5b-8e65-22276f589036","author":{"role":"assistant","name":null,"metadata":{}},"create_time":1790234201.016767,"update_time":null,"content":{"content_type":"reasoning_recap","content":"Worked for 10m 20s"},"status":"finished_successfully","end_turn":false,"weight":1.0,"metadata":{"reasoning_status":"reasoning_ended"},"recipient":"all","channel":null},{"id":"fab95594-f289-4a5f-857e-02599d6b960c","author":{"role":"assistant","name":null,"metadata":{"real_author":"tool:web"}},"create_time":1790233880.657841,"update_time":null,"content":{"content_type":"text","parts":[]},"status":"finished_successfully","end_turn":true,"weight":1.0,"metadata":{"search_result_groups":[{"domain":"github.com","entries":[{"url":"https://github.com/DTALEX66/ArcheAxis-Knowledge-OS/blob/main/README.md?utm_source=chatgpt.com"},{"url":"https://github.com/DTALEX66/ArcheAxis-Knowledge-OS/blob/main/docs/taskpacks/MANDATORY_CAPABILITY_FIRST_KNOWLEDGE_LIFECYCLE_ADDENDUM_v1_2026-08-09.md?utm_source=chatgpt.com"},{"url":"https://github.com/DTALEX66/ArcheAxis-Knowledge-OS/blob/main/docs/truth/EXECUTION_STATUS_LOG.md?utm_source=chatgpt.com"},{"url":"https://github.com/DTALEX66/ArcheAxis-Knowledge-OS/blob/main/docs/ABSORPTION_OBSIDIAN_ASSISTANCE_2026-07-13.md?utm_source=chatgpt.com"},{"url":"https://github.com/DTALEX66/ArcheAxis-Knowledge-OS/blob/main/docs/RELEASE_LEDGER.md?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}]},{"domain":"noratr.app","entries":[{"url":"https://gitblind.noratr.app/topics/evidence-driven?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}]},{"domain":"charlieautomates.com","entries":[{"url":"https://www.charlieautomates.com/free-resources/?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}]},{"domain":"osric.uk","entries":[{"url":"https://osric.uk/blog?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}]},{"domain":"jayleekr.github.io","entries":[{"url":"https://jayleekr.github.io/blog/techsavvy/ai/2025-07-10-ai-stuff/?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}]},{"domain":"lipovcan.cz","entries":[{"url":"https://git.lipovcan.cz/Upstream/bitwarden-browser/compare/vault/PM-26200..tools/PM-40120-send-access-token-should-consider-api-url?utm_source=chatgpt.com"},{"url":"https://git.lipovcan.cz/Upstream/bitwarden-browser/compare/tools/PM-40120-send-access-t